2. **Kivenson et al. (2025)** — *Science*  
   - **Title:** An archaeal genetic code with all TAG codons as pyrrolysine  
   - **Authors:** Veronika Kivenson, Samantha L. Peters, Guillaume Borrel, Aleksandr Kivenson, Leah T. Roe, et al., Jillian F. Banfield  
   - **DOI:** [`10.1126/science.adu2404`](https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adu2404) | [bioRxiv Preprint](https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.09.30.615893)  
   - **Local Full Text:** [`Kivenson_2025_archaeal_pyrrolysine_code34_Science_biorxiv.pdf`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/04_lineage_accessory/Kivenson_2025_archaeal_pyrrolysine_code34_Science_biorxiv.pdf) (3.6 MB)  
   - **Access Status:** `verified_full_text_pdf` | **Already Cited:** No  
   - **Claim & Limitation for P4:** Established Genetic Code 34 (all TAG codons encode pyrrolysine). If soil Thermoplasmatota use Code 34, Pyrodigal Table 11 prematurely truncates genes, generating artificial $<100$ aa "dark" fragments.

