## Actionable Integration Steps for P4

1. **Section 1.2 / Methods (Gene Calling & Genetic Codes):**  
   Add a direct citation to [Kivenson et al. (2025)](https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adu2404) and [Borges et al. (2022)](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04715-x). Explicitly state that while Pyrodigal ran under Table 11, the discovery of Code 34 in uncultivated Archaea highlights that stop-codon recoding could theoretically cause premature terminations, and note that P4's frame-shifted null ($dN/dS = 1.087$ vs. $0.425$) confirms purifying selection in the annotated frame.
2. **Section 2.1 / Section 3.1 (Reference Gap):**  
   Cite [Albright & Louca (2023)](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-01994-7) to anchor the 55.6% no-KO ceiling as an established structural feature of global reference databases rather than an assembly defect.
3. **Section 1.4 / Discussion (Thermoplasmatota Rarity Defense):**  
   Directly cite [Maeke et al. (2025)](https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-025-02140-8) and explain that while they attributed high unknown gene content in *Ca.* Penumbrarchaeia to environmental rarity, P4's 1:1 nearest-neighbor matched null rules out abundance, prevalence, and completeness as explanatory factors.
4. **Section 1.3 / Discussion (MAG vs. Cultivated Strain Comparison):**  
   Cite [Pellegrinetti et al. (2026)](https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2026.1884628) and [Hellewell et al. (2024)](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btae542) when interpreting the 80% annotated vs. 16% dark overlap, stating clearly that the cultivated comparison reaches only 23 bacterial species (zero Archaea) and that MAG incompleteness naturally accentuates accessory divergence.
